# Yuma AIA-A13: AI crawlers and agents enumerating a public app, or probes for MCP / LLM / agent-card endpoints
# Source: AWS WAF logs in CloudWatch Logs (log group name must start with aws-waf-logs-).
# Fields (documented): timestamp, action, terminatingRuleId, httpRequest.clientIp, httpRequest.country,
#   httpRequest.uri, httpRequest.httpMethod, labels[].name, ja4Fingerprint
#   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/logging-fields.html
# Bot Control labels AI bots (awswaf:managed:aws:bot-control:bot:category:ai, ...:bot:verified, ...:bot:name:<name>,
# ...:bot:web_bot_auth:<status>) and rule CategoryAI blocks them by default:
#   https://docs.aws.amazon.com/waf/latest/developerguide/aws-managed-rule-groups-bot.html
# This query adds what Bot Control does not: AI-agent probing of MCP and LLM paths from any client, labelled or not.
# Endpoint path list is a heuristic starter set.
fields @timestamp, httpRequest.clientIp as ip, httpRequest.country as country, httpRequest.uri as uri, action, ja4Fingerprint as ja4
| parse @message /"name":"awswaf:managed:aws:bot-control:bot:name:(?<botName>[^"]+)"/
| filter @message like /bot:category:ai/
    or uri like /(?i)^\/(mcp|sse|messages|\.well-known\/(oauth-protected-resource|oauth-authorization-server|agent\.json|agent-card\.json|ai-plugin\.json|mcp)|v1\/(chat\/completions|completions|messages|models|responses|embeddings)|api\/(generate|chat|tags)|openapi\.json)/
| stats count(*) as requests, countDistinct(uri) as uris, latest(action) as lastAction, earliest(@timestamp) as firstSeen
        by ip, country, botName, ja4
| sort requests desc
| limit 500
